  "agent_descriptions": [],
  "final": "`GET /files/<name>` now works. A signed-in user gets the raw contents of their own file as `text/plain; charset=utf-8`, with `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`. All 7 tests pass, including 4 new ones.\n\n- **Auth:** no token or a bad token returns 401, same as the other routes.\n- **Other users' files:** a file name that exists only under another user returns 404, not 403. Files are looked up only in the caller's own directory, and a 404 doesn't reveal whether the name exists for someone else.\n- **Path safety:** names go through the same `valid_name` check as uploads. `..`, dotfiles, names containing `/` or `\\`, and the empty name all return 404, and so do names containing a NUL byte. The tests check these.\n- **Where:** the new `storage.read()` is in `files_app/storage.py`, and the route is in `files_app/app.py`. The new tests are in `tests/test_app.py`, and I added a line to the README.\n\nThe first `cd` failed because the `#` in the directory name broke the path, but the shell was already in the right place, so nothing was affected.",
